{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131000-overpowered-artefacts","id":1131000,"title":"Overpowered Artefacts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-18T16:12:37-07:00","id":1131000,"title":"Overpowered Artefacts","content":"<br /> Just a query for a first time post.<br /> <br /> <br /> Just looking to figure out how many dots I'd need for an Artefact merit or even if what I want to do is game legal. Aiming to take a great sword as per Hurt Locker. And have it apply the spell effects from Life 3's Honing the Form and Forces 2's Kinetic Blow. The weapon is largely a McGuffin for plot reasons and situational as all heck like a big honking sword would be normally.<br /> <br /> Fairly certain per the spells alone make for a minimum of a 4 dot merit without any reaches.<br /> <br /> However it's with potency and reach that's getting me stumped. I'd like to max the potency on both spells to 5 Strength on Honing and +5 Damage on the Kinetic Blow. And with that comes the reaches needed to do it. I'd need Instant Cast, pushing attributes past 5, and applying Kinetic Blow to a weapon. 3 reaches at a minimum. 4 if I add Scene Duration.<br /> <br /> As a 4-dot artefact it would have a Gnosis of 2 and a Mana pool of 8.<br /> <br /> So what I'm trying to figure out is how legal this would be for 4 dots? What would have to go to keep it legal at 4 dots. How much Potency can be sacrificed. (The Reaching for attributes and applying to a weapon are the ones that need to stay or the whole thing is moot) Or how many dots it's take to make it legal in it's stupidly overpowered glory?<br /> <br /> Assuming I made sense in that, thanks for any assistance.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14593-dizzy-wuff","name":"Dizzy Wuff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14593_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T16:53:42-07:00","id":1131011,"title":"","content":"If you really want this item for a plot device and it isn't an item the players can take as a merit at character creation, then you could keep the dot level down by dividing it into two separate yet conjoined artifacts. For example the Honing could come from the cross hilt, while the extra damage comes from the blade.<br /> Don't forget that making it out of a perfected metal might also net you the advantage you want while also giving it flavor.<br /> \u200bIn the end I say do what you need for the plot and worry about how to make it work within the rules if and when that really matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T17:03:30-07:00","id":1131014,"title":"","content":"An artifact's spells don't have a set potency. You can use whatever factors you like and apply as much reach as you want. On their own they can only use free reach though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T01:29:07-07:00","id":1131160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dizzy Wuff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131000-overpowered-artefacts#post1131000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a query for a first time post.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Assuming I made sense in that, thanks for any assistance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Low dice pools and needing spell factors means stupidly low dice pools for artifacts and imbued items. One assumes you determine the spell factors on a per use basis (nothing about it in the text) and so +5 strength, +5 weapon damage is at least -16 dice (+4 potency both spells?) plus a stupid amount of over reach which may not even be possible using the free reach/s the artifact gets. (Does kinetic blow get 1 or 2 reaches? 2 because of the 3 dot honing spell seems odd?). -16 is probably not possible remembering that anything below a -5 dicepool is impossible on the 5 dicepool the item has.)<br /> <br /> As you have worked out, creating artifacts and imbued items that work well (ie need a decent potency to break withstand ratings, last for any amount of time) isnt really possible, unless the intent was to only activate them with the steadfast and informed conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 08-19-2017, 04:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T02:56:04-07:00","id":1131171,"title":"","content":"Well, Artifacts explicitly get gnosis equal to half their merit cost and arcarna equal to the the minimum required to cast all their spells. If they have a life 3 spell their life 2 spell will get two free reaches. And a mage can go over. The &quot;Free reach only&quot; thing only applies when the artifact activates itself.<br /> <br /> But yeah, there are a few issues with the way imbued items work now. I think they might be supposed to be loaded with a <i>particular </i>imago with all the stuff already set, but there's nothing in the merit regulating this so you could get crazy spells that way without much work. On the other hand the Imbue Item attainment explicitly lets you make a spell run continuously, and there's nothing in the merit about that either. That mode would <i>definitely</i> require pre-set factors.<br /> <br /> Hopefully Signs of Sorcery will re-hash them in a way that's more... functional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}